      "id": "s_story",
      "type": "story",
      "preset": "Picture right",
      "settings": {
        "image": "as_3x2_2",
        "image_side": "right",
        "body": "<p>In 2014 twelve runners met in the car park behind Foundry Lane every Saturday at eight. No kit, no fees, just a loop of the river and coffee after.</p><p>The first barbell arrived a year later, in a lock-up beside the bike shop. Since then it has grown to two rooms, six coaches and seventy-five classes a week, and the Saturday run still leaves from the river gate.</p>",
        "color_scheme": "white",
        "kicker": "Our story",
        "heading": "A gym that started as a run club"
      },
      "blocks": []
    },
